        "original_id": "88067d6d-7828-52c1-8c15-e8fe3781ba8e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Thésée\n- People: Jean-Baptiste Lully, Philippe Quinault, Ovid, Louis XIV\n- Concepts: tragédie en musique, French opera\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was born as Giovanni Battista Lulli on 28 November 1632 and became an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully spent most of his life working at the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Thésée is a tragédie en musique, an early type of French opera, structured as a prologue and five acts.\n- Thésée has music by Jean-Baptiste Lully and a libretto by Philippe Quinault.\n- Thésée is based on Ovid's Metamorphoses.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully died on 22 March 1687.",
